[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Business Requirements
UID: YAAP-BR
DATE: @GIT_COMMIT_DATETIME
PREFIX: BR-

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Introduction

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document defines the business requirements for Yet Another Audio Player (Yaap),
a time accurate desktop audio player.

Yaap provides users with an audio library and playback experience.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Audio Playback

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Supported Audio Playback

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-001
TITLE: Supported audio
STATEMENT: >>>
Yaap shall support playback of a range of audio formats and codecs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-002
TITLE: Audio Playback Stored Locally
STATEMENT: >>>
Yaap shall provide the ability to play supported audio files stored locally on their
devices.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-003
TITLE: Audio Playback Stored Externally
STATEMENT: >>>
Yaap shall provide the ability to play supported audio files stored on supported,
linked cloud providers.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Audio Playback Functionality

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-004
TITLE: Audio Playback Quality
STATEMENT: >>>
Yaap shall provide accurate audio playback appropriate for high-quality audio
collections.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-005
TITLE: Audio Playback Position
STATEMENT: >>>
Yaap shall provide an accurate representation of the current or requested playback
position of an audio track.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-006
TITLE: Audio Playback Customization
STATEMENT: >>>
Yaap shall allow for playback characteristic customizations such as speed, pitch,
volume, and audio processing.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Organisation

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Audio Library

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-007
TITLE: Audio Library
STATEMENT: Yaap shall provide a persistent library containing supported audio tracks.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-008
TITLE: Searching, Sorting and Filtering
STATEMENT: Yaap shall allow for searching, sorting and filtering of tracks.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Track Metadata

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-009
TITLE: Audio Metadata
STATEMENT: >>>
Yaap shall allow for the viewing, managing, and where appropriate modification of
track metadata.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Library Activity

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-010
TITLE: Activity
STATEMENT: Yaap shall provide library activity information.

[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Queue, Playlist and Collection Management

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-011
TITLE: Playlist and Collection Organisation
STATEMENT: >>>
Yaap shall allow for the creation, modification and organisation of
playlists and collections.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-012
TITLE: Playback Queue
STATEMENT: Yaap shall be able to create and modify its playback queue.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-013
TITLE: Playback Control
STATEMENT: Yaap shall allow users to control the order of tracks being played.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Personalisation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-014
TITLE: User Preferences
STATEMENT: >>>
Yaap shall allow users to configure application and playback settings.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-015
TITLE: Internationalisation
STATEMENT: Yaap shall allow for the application language to be changed.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Analytics

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-016
TITLE: Listening Analytics
STATEMENT: >>>
Yaap shall allow for the analysis of listening behaviour and audio consumption.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Interoperability

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-017
TITLE: Sharing 
STATEMENT: Yaap shall allow for the sharing of playlists and collections.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: User Interaction

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-018
TITLE: Interaction Modes
STATEMENT: >>>
Yaap shall provide access to functionality through graphical, terminal,
and command-line interfaces.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Data Management

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-019
TITLE: Operation Recovery
STATEMENT: Yaap shall allow reversible modifications to be undone and redone.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: BR-020
TITLE: User Data Persistence
STATEMENT: Yaap shall persist user-created information between sessions.

[[/SECTION]]
